            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_70f01d22">B2:422</identifier>
            <title xml:id="_19" xml:lang="da">Kantate, da den durchlauchtigste og høibaarne Enke-Fyrstinde af Ostfriesland, hendes Liig hensattes i de kongelige Begravelser i Roeskilde</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_8df4c537">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_21">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
               <persName role="author" xml:id="_23">Niels Prahl</persName>
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="_22">Princess Sophia Carolina of Ost-Friesland</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_24_0">
               <date isodate="1764" xml:id="date_7d748766">1764</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_24_0">Copenhagen,</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_24_0">
               <p xml:id="idm123">When the sister of the queen dowager, <persName xml:id="idm124" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Princess Sophia Carolina of Ost-Friesland</persName>, died in the early summer of 1764, Scheibe was asked to compose the present mourning cantata to a text by <persName xml:id="idm125" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Niels Prahl</persName>. On the 27 June at eight in the evening, the funeral procession left the deceased princess' residens Sorgenfri north of Copenhagen, arriving in Roskilde at six in the morning on the following day. The service took place in Roskilde Cathedral and according to the newspaper,<rend xml:id="idm126" fontstyle="italic"> Kiøbenhavns Adresse-Contoirs Efterretninger</rend>, Scheibe led the performance. The funeral oration was held by <persName xml:id="idm127" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Josias Lorck</persName>. The music has since been lost. The text was published in the previously mentioned newspaper thus suggesting that a printed libretto was not issued for the event; but the following year both funeral oration, a description of the event and of Sophia Carolina's last days as well as the libretto were published. The description mentions that 'as soon as the service began in the church, The Royal Orchestra led by mr Kapellmeister Scheibe played a well-composed funeral music in Danish of which I [i.e. Lorck] have contributed with the text of the speech. When this sad service had ended and the music ceased, all retired without further ceremony to the royal palace in Roskilde, where the royal kitchen gave a splendid supper at various tables, at one of which a delightful dessert was fashioned according to this sad event, representing the virtues of the late lamented princess' (p. 29). In the newspaper, <rend xml:id="idm128" fontstyle="italic">Kiøbenhavnske danske Post-Tidender</rend>, the whole event is described in detail, mentioning that the mourning cantata, which was very beautiful, was led by Kapellmeister Scheibe with such common praise (‘saa almindeligt Bifald’) that it did both him and The Royal Orchestra great honour as well as the well known poet.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_38cabe39">
               <language xml:id="da">Danish</language>
            </langUsage>
